# Standard Quality Clean Test Deploy

## Testing Requirements

- **All tests MUST pass (100% pass rate)** – Failing tests are noise that obscure real issues.
- **NEVER skip fixing failing tests** – Always fix before proceeding.
- **Run tests and report results** – Do not claim pass without evidence.
- **Use proper test frameworks** – Create `*.test.ts` files, not ad-hoc scripts.

## Clean Requirements

- **Fix introduced lint and type errors** – No new warnings or errors.
- **Remove temporary artifacts** – Delete `.temp/` files, debug code, unused imports.
- **No commented-out code** – Delete it; git preserves history.
- **Consistent formatting** – Follow project conventions.

## Code Review

**AI agents MUST perform code review before completion:**

Review for:
- Type safety (no `any`, proper interfaces)
- Security (input validation, no secrets)
- Performance (no N+1, proper memoization)
- Accessibility (ARIA, semantic HTML, keyboard)
- Error handling (try/catch, user-facing messages)
- Testing (coverage, edge cases)

## Documentation

- Document notable risks, tradeoffs, or deferred work
- Update user-facing docs for behavior changes
- Add comments for non-obvious logic (explain "why", not "what")
